  "change": {
    "kind": "compare",
    "base": "main",
    "head": "scenario/dj02-method-decorator"
  },
  "explains": "invoice_detail in billing/views.py changes (its body). It is a function view with @require_http_methods([\"GET\", \"PUT\"]), so one view gives two routes, one per method, and no route for the others. Both are mounted by the same path() line, path(\"invoices/<int:invoice_id>/\", ...): the converter <int:invoice_id> is the parameter {invoice_id}, under billing/ from config/urls.py. Full path: /billing/invoices/{invoice_id}, as GET and as PUT. The web client calls it with apiGet(invoiceUrl(invoiceId)), a GET with a parameter segment, which fits the GET route; nothing calls the PUT route. invoiceUrl is used by fetchInvoice, which InvoiceDetailPage calls, mounted at /billing/invoices/:invoiceId. voidInvoice posts to /billing/invoices/{id}/void/, a different route, so it is not an edge of this change. As in dj01, config/urls.py imports the module for another name and is excluded; billing/urls.py is the caller.",
